# Recordings. A sample library's licence covers what is rendered from it, and
# audio captured from a tone generator is the machine's ROM content. Measured
# values are committed; the audio they came from is not.
*.wav
*.aiff
*.flac
takes-manifest.json
.cache/
captures/

# Published documents. The copyright in one is somebody else's, so the file is
# never committed -- what is committed is the factual content of its tables,
# under documents/, cited by printed page. .documents/ is where the files sit
# while they are read, and the extension is ignored alongside it, because the
# guard that matters is the one that still holds when a copy lands somewhere
# else by mistake. That is a directory a dot away from the tracked one.
*.pdf
.documents/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Working documents. Plans, records and running notes live here; only the
# archive and the harness are tracked. What is measured goes in data/, what
# is decided goes here. A driver that is specific to one unit stays here; one
# that is part of the protocol belongs in procedures/, which is tracked, because
# a second unit measured by a script nobody else has is not measured the same way.
backup/

# Local agent configuration. Instructions to whoever or whatever is working on
# this, and the state its tooling keeps. It describes neither the unit nor the
# harness, so it stays out of both.
.claude/
.claude-*/
CLAUDE.md
.codex/
AGENTS.md
AGENT.md
.serena/
.mcp.json
